  "policy_notes": "2.2.0: entry cooldown after the 31 Aug duplicate fills (four entries on one setup, 16.53 of a 51.46 loss). Watcher stop buffer 250->600 and a FIXED 400pt target rather than a multiple of the stop. Hourly swing levels as a zone source when the dashboard sends none. Measured over 48,488 M1 bars of Aug 2026: zone entry at an hourly level returned +0.024R against -0.223R for the same geometry entered arbitrarily. Shorter entry windows beat longer ones \u2014 8h over 24h at every buffer, because more time gives price more chances to reach the stop. 2.3.0: gates now reason about TOTAL cost, not spread. XM charges 40pts of spread and no commission (0.051% of notional). Binance quotes a 0.01 spread and charges 0.1% per side, which is ~157pts on the same notional \u2014 four times more expensive. Judging a venue by its spread alone gets one of these badly wrong.",
